WEBVTT

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.030
<b>Skull-face Bookseller Honda-san</b>

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.040
<b>An Outstanding Bookseller</b>

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:09.620
<i>Working at a bookstore, we sometimes 
receive questions like this one:</i>

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:13.680
<b>What kind of person is a good fit
 for work at a bookstore?</b>

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.660
Who's good for working at a bookstore?

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.160
That's what I'd like to know.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.440
What would you answer, Honda-san?

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.810
Um...

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:32.330
<b>*Personal opinion</b>

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.980
Someone who doesn't care about being 
monetarily rewarded for their work,

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:29.300
who can control their expressive 
muscles to a certain degree,

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.140
and is reasonably sociable.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:35.800
Stop that, please!

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:38.400
Especially the part about monetary rewards!

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.390
I want more pay!

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:41.880
I mean, I get it, but...

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:42.900
Pipe down.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.380
And don't talk about your fetishes.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:46.470
We were talking about work!

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:50.420
I thought you were going to say, like, 
"someone who can speak English."

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:53.640
Someone like that is also suitable 
for places other than bookstores.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.960
Oh, speaking of which, there's 
something I noticed recently...

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:02.640
Bookstores are perpetually 
organizing something or other.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:04.670
<b>*Personal opinion</b>

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:03.940
That's true.

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:07.200
We pull out new books and make returns...

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:10.800
Return

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.390
Every day is spent pulling things 
out and putting things in.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:14.640
The book stacks tend to end 
up looking like bar graphs.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:14.740
<b>Ideally</b>

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.170
And the magazines end up looking
 like the katakana "no" and "shi."

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:20.050
<b>In a perfect world</b>

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.360
That's never a good thing.

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:24.280
<b>I caught a shoplifter</b>

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:24.280
<b>Products</b>

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:24.280
Shoplifters tend to prey 
on disorganized shelves.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:30.090
<b>Social Order</b>

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:28.570
And the social order type people 
tend to get on our case.

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:30.090
Oh, no!

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.740
I'm gonna work my hardest
 to keep things in order!

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:34.220
Yeah, let's do it!

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:39.000
<i>But that's easier said than done.</i>

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:43.090
<i>The shelves end up disorderly in no time.</i>

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:46.410
<b>Bam</b>

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:47.870
<b>Woosh</b>

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:49.540
<b>Ta-da</b>

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.280
<i>These shelves...</i>

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:53.720
<i>Sneak.</i>

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:54.720
<i>Sneak.</i>

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:55.800
<i>Sneak, sneak, sneak.</i>

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:05.050
<i>Each publisher is sorted and stocked 
by author and grouped by volume count!</i>

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:07.700
Hey, what's up?

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:10.040
Are you looking for something?

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:12.460
N-No, I'm not looking for anything.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:13.670
I was just peeking.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.000
Why are you doing that?!

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.560
Gotta go, bye!

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:19.360
<i>I'm humbled.</i>

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:22.530
<i>Fullface-senpai is something else.</i>

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.240
<b>Staff Only</b>

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.240
I know, right?!

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:29.060
It's not just the shelves. His personal 
drawers are always tidy as hell.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:31.580
Dude, your shelves are super clean, too!

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:35.020
The chaos at my place is, like, 
<i>Mad**x</i> level, to put it lightly.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:39.130
Why don't we get Fullface-san 
to do our shelves, too?

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.660
That's tempting, but no thanks.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:43.420
Seriously, put a sock in it.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:44.930
We're sorry.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:51.940
Oh, man. Wow. Fullface-san 
cleaned up my spot, huh?

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:53.930
How did you know?

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:57.630
It's organized in a way 
that's logical to anyone,

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:00.800
it's orderly, and it's easy to understand.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.510
No one else can maintain such a state.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.100
Not anyone here, at least.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:08.120
Dude! You're right, but come on!

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.460
Say something, Manager!

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:11.990
I can't.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.380
You're so loud.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:15.740
There he is.

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:21.160
We were just talking about how your area 
is so tidy, even including your stock.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.330
Tidy?

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:24.430
Tidy, huh?

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:27.340
I mean, I'm cleaning for my own sake,

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:30.490
but it makes things easier for everyone 
when it's easy to find stock.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:33.240
It sucks when we have to dig
 through all of it, right?

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:36.190
That's our Fullface.

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:38.520
A true bookseller.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.550
Nah, I'm just doing what's normal.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:43.570
Stop it! You're just rubbing it in!

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:46.360
<i>A person who can act in the interest of others</i>

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:48.700
<i>is the kind of person a bookstore needs.</i>

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:51.690
<i>Isn't that right, Senpai?</i>

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.860
<b>*Personal opinion</b>

00:04:55.970 --> 00:04:57.640
Section Chief Pestmask.

00:04:57.640 --> 00:04:59.200
Yes?

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:03.380
What kind of person comes to mind when 
you think of good bookseller material?

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:05.880
Where did that come from?

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.720
I don't know.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:10.920
There are a lot, but...

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:19.710
<b>*Personal opinion</b>

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:14.090
Someone who doesn't steal
 or become violent...

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:18.680
Someone who isn't asking 
to be arrested, maybe?

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.820
Oh, someone who likes books?

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:26.010
<i>You there, the hero looking 
to work at a bookstore,</i>

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:29.480
<i>it might not be too hard to get the job.</i>

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:34.030
<b>Swapping Section Heads</b>

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:43.350
Things are heating up in 
the staff shuffle meeting.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:46.150
They always seem really stumped, though.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:49.680
It decides your fate, after all.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.760
This kind of takes me back.

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:54.320
<b>A few years ago</b>

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:54.320
** Bookstore

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:56.870
Looks like it isn't a full shuffle this time.

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:58.730
I wanna switch.

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:01.030
Gimme something really easy.

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:05.450
In any case, Honda-san, you'll 
be in charge of something else.

00:06:05.450 --> 00:06:06.310
Oh, my!

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:10.110
Honda-san, you've been in charge 
of the current section for a while,

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:13.080
so we decided you should try something new.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:14.130
Congrats.

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:19.480
Oh, err, I'm just busy thinking about how I <i>really</i> 
need to clean my shelves before we switch.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:20.620
You're so proper.

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:24.590
Are there any sections you're 
interested in, Honda?

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:25.360
Nope.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:26.520
That was quick.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:28.970
There are some sections I don't want...

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:31.690
Ones that I don't have 
the confidence to handle.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:33.660
I think we might be the same.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:34.550
Which section?

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.460
The gaming stuff.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.700
Same!

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:42.900
It's not that I have contempt for 
gaming magazines or anything...

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:44.640
If anything, it's the other
 way around! I know!

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:55.610
<b>What's this? I smell a noob in the shelves.</b>

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.810
We're not gamers at all,

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:50.590
so the customers tend to know more 
about the strategy guides and stuff.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:52.830
I feel like the customers can tell right away

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:55.610
when someone who doesn't know 
the content is managing the shelves.

00:06:55.810 --> 00:07:00.050
I mean, it's work, so I'll do it 
begrudgingly if I have to.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:03.340
But I can't imagine I'd accomplish much 
aside from ruining our sales numbers.

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:04.250
<i>I know.</i>

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:07.130
<i>I know, but Kamibukuro-senpai,</i>

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:10.670
<i>at the end of the day, you're 
hard-working, tough, and capable.</i>

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:12.360
<i>Even though you're weird.</i>

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:14.410
<i>I'm not saying that the gaming shelves</i>

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:18.280
<i>are the only ones I can't handle.</i>

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:22.950
<i>I have no confidence with </i>any<i> 
of the well-known publishers!</i>

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:27.110
<b>What follows is Honda's strictly personal 
opinions on sorting shelves by publisher.</b>

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:39.160
<b>Shu-E-sha</b>

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.140
<i>Let's go!</i>

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:31.200
<i>First, the king of manga, Shu-E-sha!</i>

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:35.120
<i>The popular series never end, and they 
keep selling even after they finish,</i>

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:37.180
<i>so they can't be removed from the shops.</i>

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:39.160
<i>A shelf from Hell!</i>

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:41.740
<i>Kou-D-sha is picking up steam!</i>

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:47.430
<b>Kou-D-sha</b>

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:44.130
<i>A mad publisher that finds a strange pleasure</i>

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:47.430
<i>in shortening each title's 
frequency of new releases.</i>

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:55.070
<b>Sho-G-kan</b>

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:49.900
<i>The eternal final boss, Sho-G-kan!</i>

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:55.070
<i>A super-duper proper publisher that'll 
never accept an order unless you fax them!</i>

00:07:55.070 --> 00:08:02.840
<b>Shonen-G-housha</b>

00:07:55.070 --> 00:08:02.840
<b>Aki-T-shoten</b>

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:57.750
<i>Aki-T-shoten and Shonen-G-housha!</i>

00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:00.460
<i>Many of their customers demand 
blood, guts, and comedy,</i>

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:02.840
<i>so we have to keep their shelves extra tidy!</i>

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:12.990
<b>Toku-M-shoten</b>

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:12.990
<b>Shin-C-sha</b>

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.180
<i>Toku-M-shoten and Shin-C-sha!</i>

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:08.960
<i>There's such huge fluctuation 
in interest for their titles!</i>

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:12.550
<i>Let your guard down, and they'll create a 
buzz online, leaving us with nothing in stock!</i>

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:15.240
<i>Welcome to chaos: Haku-S-sha!</i>

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:23.530
<b>Haku-S-sha</b>

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:18.350
<i>The lack of consistency in the 
moods they set is unrivaled!</i>

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:23.100
<i>Their section is best led by someone who can 
quickly add stock as soon as a new book releases!</i>

00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:26.770
<i>And the most terrifying of them all...</i>

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:30.810
<i>The multi-headed publishing 
lifeform colony, KADOKAWA.</i>

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:33.740
<i>Perhaps their goal is to fill the calendar 
with their own comic launches,</i>

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.650
<i>but there's a new volume every day.</i>

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:38.350
<i>The New Book Instrumentality Project!</i>

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:40.610
<i>They're just really slow to reprint books.</i>

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:41.940
<i></i>Seriously<i> slow!</i>

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:45.270
<i>So we end up ordering more 
than we expect to sell.</i>

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:49.060
<i>This, too, may be part of 
the Instrumentality Project.</i>

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:53.700
<i>I'm starting to hate—I mean,</i>

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:56.730
<i>lose confidence in—all the shelves.</i>

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:57.680
<i>No, no, no!</i>

00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:59.020
<i>Buck up, Honda.</i>

00:08:59.020 --> 00:08:59.600
<i>It's all right.</i>

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:04.240
<b>*Artist rendition</b>

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:03.870
<i>So long as they don't throw me a huge 
curveball, there's no section I can't handle!</i>

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:06.010
<b>New person in charge: Honda</b>

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:06.010
<b>American Comics 
Oversized books</b>

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:06.010
<b>Previously in charge: Houtai</b>

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:06.010
<b>Please soldier on ❤ by Armor</b>

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:09.070
You got this!

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:11.440
#^(*&@%#(*&!

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:14.110
I don't read American comics! I have no idea!

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:15.420
You'll be fine.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:19.590
<b>Used Cardboard</b>

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:19.590
I didn't either, but keep 
at it and you'll make it!

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:23.430
Foreign comics and other big books get 
treated more like books than manga,

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:25.620
so just randomly arrange them.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:28.120
It's perfect for half-assers like you and me.

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:29.860
<i>Your true colors are showing.</i>

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:34.780
But, I feel like the customers can tell

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:37.010
whether or not I have as much 
passion as you do.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:44.240
<b>I dunno</b>

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:40.900
You'll end up loving them 
eventually, I guess.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.080
<i>So half-assed!</i>

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:45.710
You'll get used to it.

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:47.920
I'll back you up in the beginning.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.830
Thank you.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:53.950
<i>I was worried about the 
foreign comics shelves,</i>

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:57.360
<i>but strangely, I'm still in charge.</i>

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:01.040
<i>I don't know whether I'm good at it or not,</i>

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:05.060
<i>but it's true that it's grown 
on me since I started.</i>

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:08.270
<b>Newly in-charge: Kendo</b>

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:08.270
<b>Magazine-style comics</b>

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:09.710
And so, you're in charge now.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:11.490
Magazine-style comics, huh?

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:13.360
That sounds really hard.

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:14.430
Don't worry!

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:16.270
You can learn about them as you go.

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:21.860
Life is all about trying new things, huh?

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:25.780
Should I stop being fussy 
and try the gaming shelves?

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:28.790
I'll be waiting!

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:30.990
In charge of gaming
